      "decision": "INCLUDE",
      "primary_reason": "All six eligibility gates are YES: primary 15-page peer-reviewed IEEE Access article (published 20 May 2025, in English) evaluating distributed CNN layer partitioning and trajectory optimization across multi-UAV swarms in simulation.",
      "evaluation_modes": [
        "simulation"
      ],
      "alignment": {
        "category": "core_orchestration",
        "rationale": "Jointly orchestrates sequential CNN layer assignment across UAVs, 3D UAV trajectory planning, reliable data-rate/power constraints, and online adaptation when UAVs join, leave for recharging, or change memory capacity.",
        "page": 1,
        "quote": "To address these issues, we formulate the problem of CNN layer distribution and UAV trajectory planning (LDTP) as an optimization problem to improve latency, reliability, and resource usage."
      },
      "unresolved": [
        "Potential study-family lineage with prior Dhuheir et al. multi-UAV CNN distributed-inference papers cited in Section II (Refs. [8], [27], [30]: IWCMC 2021 [S01], WCNC 2023, IEEE IoT J. 2023), requiring verification of distinctness in the study-to-report map.",
        "Minor unit inconsistency in Section VI-A (p. 10), which states Raspberry Pi B+ devices support 'different multiplication rates per second (560 MB, 512 MB, and 256 MB)' before describing those values as memory capacities in Section VI-B4.",
        "Simulation-only evaluation without physical multi-UAV flight testing or real-world CNN inference accuracy evaluation under link losses."
